
ED - The Advanced Configurable Editor. Demonstration Version 2.01  10 Aug 93
============================================================================

This is a Demonstration Copy of the third release of the award winning
Windows version of "ED - The Advanced Configurable Editor".  

Please note that a major upgrade to ED for DOS is nearing completion and
incorporates all the features of this release of ED for Windows.

This release includes some important new features which keep ED as the
leader of the pack for professional programmer's editors. 

In particular language support has been extended considerably to include
Cobol, Fortran, Paradox, Progress, Pascal, Lisp, Assembler, DataFlex,
FoxPro and SQL as well as C/C++, Clipper/dBase etc.

Color Syntax highlighting has been added which goes way beyond similar
features in other products. Sixteen base item categories are provided
including: comments, preprocessor statements, strings, hex, octal and
decimal numbers, keywords, whitespace etc. In addition you can specify
your own separate lists of words for each language in a simple ASCII
text file and associate colors for each list.

File difference analysis lets you compare files. Any differences are
highlighted with simultaneous scrolling through both files in separate
windows.

A Ruler can be displayed at the current cursor location. This quickly
lets you find the number of characters in a string.

ED's dialog boxes now have a jazzy 3D look.

The on line help has been extended and improved, making it easier to
find information.

ED now keeps track of original line numbers so compiler error tracking
now works even after lines have been inserted or deleted.

Bracket matching ignores brackets inside comments and strings so you end
up on the correct bracket at all times.

Code Templates have been extended and can now optionally be expanded
with the Space bar in addition to the K_TEMPLATE command. The template
programs have been rewritten making it easier to add or change
templates,

Template expansion using the Space bar no longer occurs inside
comments.

A new option has been added which prevents ED from restoring to the
directory it was in when last run. This lets you have separate ED icons
in the Program Manager ED group, with each one starting ED in a
different working directory.

dBase/Clipper programmers can now access DBF file field information by
using Goto|Locate Object on a USE, DBUSEAREA or SELECT statement.
Alternatively you can use Tool|Execute ED Program DBF_GETS at any time. 

Paradox for Windows developers can right click on any Paradox keyword
and get context sensitive help.


This release also incorporates as many enhancements and problem fixes as
possible that have been requested since the second release.

Please read the file READ.ME for a summary of new features and enhancements.
Also the "What's New" topic in the on line help.



This release also incorporates as many enhancements and problem fixes as
possible that have been requested since the second release.

Please read READ.ME for a summary of new features and enhancements.

======================================================================


The Wait is Over!  AT LAST, a full featured Windows developer's
editor is HERE!

You are about to use the most powerful programmer's text editor
available today. ED is fully configurable, fully programmable
and is very easy to use. Plenty of on line help is available,
along with emulations for editors such as Brief, MultiEdit, Wordstar,
Qedit and Norton Editor. ED is available for DOS and Windows with
versions for other platforms and operating systems in progress.


